        <item>
          <title>Applying Functions with Sums of Products: The case/constr Trick and When It Actually Pays</title>
          <link>https://lantr.io/blog/plutus-v3-case-constr-function-application</link>
          <description>Plutus V3 lets you call a function through a case expression instead of nested applies, spending fewer execution units. Every major Cardano compiler now does it above two arguments. But that threshold is only half the calculation: the encoding is also bigger below seven arguments, and measurement shows five sites in six never repeat — so the decision needs a profile, not a rule of thumb.</description>
          <pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
